    "{\"description\": \"Activate a narrow tool-use lane for retrieval, math, and code-check tasks when tools/repl/react_mode are already enabled, so CALL-based execution can replace long reasoning without changing eval methodology.\", \"file\": \"src/tool_policy.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add 2-3 compliance exemplars demonstrating exact-match reformatting for the highest-yield scoring contracts: (a) code-only output starting at the first token with no fences/preamble, and (b) single-token multiple-choice answers with no surrounding prose. Keep the verbatim ordered compliance rules unchanged; only append worked examples to reduce format-induced scoring misses on code_execution and multiple_choice scored suites.\", \"file\": \"formalizer.md\", \"mutation\": \"few_shot_evolution\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add 2-3 concrete format-compliance exemplars (exact JSON with field order/casing, raw-code-only, no-fence/no-preamble cases) showing input answer -> strictly reformatted output, to lift the floored instruction_precision suite. Distinct mechanism from t779's enforcement-language tightening: give the model concrete schema-matching patterns, not more rules. Do NOT alter non-format paths or add prose verbosity.\", \"file\": \"formalizer.md\", \"mutation\": \"few_shot_evolution\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a conservative format-sensitive fallback: when a cheap/frontdoor answer is low-confidence or empty for instruction_precision, bigcodebench, usaco, or mode_advantage_hard style requests, route once to the existing specialist path without changing model selection or global feature flags.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a conservative suite-agnostic factual-QA escalation guard: when routing or answer metadata indicates low-evidence open-domain or multi-hop QA, escalate once to architect_general instead of returning the fast worker answer; do not change eval, scoring, question pools, or suite-specific logic.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a deterministic final-pass schema compliance step: before returning, if the request specifies an exact output format (JSON shape, list form, field order, casing, key names), re-emit the answer strictly conforming to that schema verbatim \\u2014 overriding any prose-wrapped draft. Do NOT alter non-format-constrained paths or lengthen general prose. Hypothesis: instruction_precision regressed 3.0->0.0 because upstream format enforcement (t779) sets intent but a final draft still wraps/deviates; a strict terminal re-emit recovers the suite without regressing already-passing suites.\", \"file\": \"formalizer.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a minimal speed-aware escalation guard so escalation only routes to architect-level paths when confidence/risk justifies the latency, preserving current quality fallback behavior while reducing unnecessary slow escalations. Do not change scoring, question pools, prompts, model registry, or eval methodology.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a narrow escalation guard for exact-answer and format-sensitive hard tasks so instruction_precision, bigcodebench, usaco, and mode_advantage_hard bypass cheap-first early exit for one specialist or architect pass; leave prompts, models, and eval files untouched.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a narrow tool-use sentinel lane in the existing tool policy so explicit retrieval, arithmetic, and code-check tasks preserve/activate the existing REPL/tool CALL path; leave non-tool tasks unchanged and do not touch eval/scoring.\", \"file\": \"src/tool_policy.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a short-factual fast path in the chat pipeline: when the request is a brief factual NL question (simpleqa/gpqa/hotpotqa shape \\u2014 single-clause, no code/format constraints), skip aggressive input formalization and context compaction that rewrites or truncates the answer-bearing query, and return the model's direct answer verbatim. Do NOT alter code/agentic/long-context paths or change routing. Hypothesis: simpleqa is pinned at 0.00 because the formalizer/compaction stages mangle or over-process short factual queries before answering; a narrow direct-answer path should lift simpleqa/gpqa/hotpotqa off the floor without regressing already-passing suites.\", \"file\": \"src/api/routes/chat.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a strict final-answer format-compliance pass to the output formalizer: when the request specifies an exact output schema (JSON shape, list form, field order, key casing, delimiters), re-emit the final answer verbatim to that schema before returning, and drop any extra prose/preamble. Do NOT lengthen general prose or alter non-format reasoning paths. Targets instruction_precision floor (0.00) without regressing already-passing suites.\", \"file\": \"formalizer.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add a strict output-format compliance pass: when a request specifies an exact schema (JSON shape, list form, field order, casing, or required fields), re-emit the final answer verbatim to that schema before returning, and verify each named constraint is satisfied. Do NOT lengthen general prose or alter non-format paths. Hypothesis: instruction_precision is floored because the formalizer under-enforces strict schema adherence; targeted final-format enforcement should lift it without regressing already-passing tool_use/coder suites.\", \"file\": \"formalizer.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add concise execution-trace reasoning guidance to the coder primary prompt to repair the cruxeval/code-execution-output hole exposed at T2 (#1038 cruxeval -1.122, livecodebench/coder declining): before emitting code or a predicted output, mentally simulate the program state step by step (variable bindings, loop iterations, control flow) and verify the result against the prompt's stated inputs. Keep it terse (1-2 bullets) to avoid token bloat; do not alter the existing 'output working code directly / be concise' instruction.\", \"file\": \"roles/coder_primary.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Add explicit final-answer discipline for graduate-level multiple-choice / short-factual reasoning (gpqa): before emitting, enumerate the candidate answers, eliminate distractors with a one-line reason each, then commit to exactly ONE best answer in the requested format. Do NOT add verbosity to non-reasoning synthesis paths, do not alter tool/coder synthesis behavior. Hypothesis: gpqa sits at its ~0.69/1.50 floor because architect synthesis hedges across options instead of committing; eliminate-then-commit discipline should lift gpqa without regressing the already-strong thinking/coder/tool_use suites.\", \"file\": \"architect_synthesis.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Align Q-scorer/frontdoor baseline throughput with measured Qwen3.5-35B moe6-only throughput of 12.7 t/s instead of the stale lookup-era 19.6 t/s value, so routing cost estimates reflect current production speed without changing model selection or eval methodology.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
