    "{\"description\": \"Audit and minimally fix prompt-resolution provenance: when resolve_prompt() loads a named prompt from orchestration/prompts/*.md, validate it against expected provenance and fall back to the known-good fallback constant when the on-disk file is empty, truncated, or fails the provenance check, instead of forwarding corrupted/leaked content to models. Single variable: resolver correctness only \\u2014 do not edit any prompt .md text, scoring, question pools, model registry, routing flags, or eval methodology.\", \"file\": \"src/prompt_builders/resolver.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Audit and minimally fix worker/specialist output propagation in the chat pipeline so a completed model response is returned to the scorer with its full text and non-empty content, instead of an empty, truncated, or unevaluated payload when a worker returns before formalization. Single variable: response-propagation correctness in chat.py only. Do NOT change scoring, question pools, model registry, routing flags, prompt files, eval methodology, or baselines.\", \"file\": \"src/api/routes/chat.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Audit resolve_prompt() and add the narrowest validity/provenance guard only for concrete invalid prompt loads: if orchestration/prompts/<name>.md is missing, unreadable, empty, or whitespace-only, fall back to the existing in-code default for that prompt name and log the fallback reason with name/path/provenance. Single variable: prompt-resolution fallback correctness in resolver.py only. Do NOT add content-shape heuristics, edit prompt text, scoring, question pools, model registry, routing flags, baselines, or eval methodology.\", \"file\": \"src/prompt_builders/resolver.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Audit the front-door ChatPipeline request path for a defect that would uniformly floor ALL T1 suites since ~t844 \\u2014 e.g. responses returned empty/truncated, the final answer field dropped before scoring, or an exception swallowed into a blank completion. Single variable: chat-route response assembly/return correctness only. Do NOT touch scoring, question pools, model registry, routing flags, prompt files, or eval methodology.\", \"file\": \"src/api/routes/chat.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
