    "{\"description\": \"Compress debugger_system.md by removing the legacy RELOAD_SERVICE/NEW_SIGNAL fallback block (fully superseded by the documented json:debugger_actions protocol) and tightening surrounding redundancy. Single-variable: lower instruction_token_ratio on debug/coder tasks while holding debugbench/coder quality non-inferior. Keepable-if-accepted, so it can serve as a fresh W8 promotion candidate that reverting structural toggles cannot.\", \"file\": \"debugger_system.md\", \"mutation\": \"compress\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Compress redundant instruction tokens in the frontdoor prompt (Tier-1 conciseness): hypothesis is the prompt carries low-info-per-token instruction blocks; a semantics-preserving compress reduces per-request decode and may push speed past the #511 frontier point (sp=61.7), targeting the open q\\u2208[1.816,1.895] gap. Rotates off the exhausted 7-deep structural_experiment lock-in onto the under-used prompt surface; PromptForge's internal quality gate self-reverts any real regression.\", \"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"mutation\": \"compress\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Compress redundant instruction tokens in the frontdoor prompt (Tier-1 conciseness, token-reducing \\u2014 the non-harmful prompt lever). Hypothesis: a semantics-preserving verbosity reduction trims per-request decode without quality loss; PromptForge's gate self-reverts any regression. Chosen as the lowest-risk clean idle because the structural-OFF flag pool degraded this turn \\u2014 staged_rewards just T1-phantom-failed #589, joining the structural negative cluster \\u2014 making prompt-surface idles safer than re-toggling a recently-failed or near-blacklist flag.\", \"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"mutation\": \"compress\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Compress redundant instruction tokens in the frontdoor prompt (Tier-1 conciseness, token-reducing \\u2014 the non-harmful prompt lever, distinct from the speed-harmful few_shot #585). Hypothesis: a semantics-preserving reduction in prompt verbosity trims per-request decode without quality loss; PromptForge's internal gate self-reverts any regression. Rotates action_type off the impending 3-consecutive-structural lock-in while idling cleanly per the convergence guard.\", \"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"mutation\": \"compress\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Compress the rules.md few-shot exemplars (168 lines): dedupe overlapping examples and tighten prose while preserving the load-bearing format lessons (FINAL() required, code-as-string for coder/debugbench, compute-first MCQ, web_research over web_search). New non-blacklisted surface after 20 gate-dominated structural/seed trials; targets avoidable prompt-token bloat and tests whether 'compress reliably passes' still holds under the current baseline regime.\", \"file\": \"rules.md\", \"mutation\": \"compress\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Content-vs-artifact discriminator for the general-suite gate block (still-open #1124/#1125/#1126/#1131). Tighten ONLY the simple/general-question path (root_lm_system.md:1 \\u2014 direct FINAL answers with exact user-formatting compliance) to raise general-suite answer correctness; do not touch the REPL/tool/code/web branches. Fork test: if general's fixed -1.800 regression moves or T1 clears the gate, the loss is content-sensitive and prompt-tunable; if general stays exactly -1.800 across this content change (as it did across 15 flag toggles 1091-1131), the block is a baseline-coverage artifact (general n_baseline=2) requiring an operator baseline refresh, not an autopilot surface.\", \"file\": \"root_lm_system.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
