    "{\"description\": \"Fix named-prompt resolution provenance: ensure resolve_prompt(name) returns the intended orchestration/prompts/<name>.md content, and on miss/empty falls back to the explicit module constant with a logged provenance tag instead of silently returning an empty or stale string. Single variable: resolver correctness only. No prompt text, scoring, question pools, model registry, routing flags, or eval methodology changes.\", \"file\": \"src/prompt_builders/resolver.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Fix prompt resolution/fallback for format-sensitive benchmark tasks so instruction_precision, bigcodebench, usaco, vl, and mode_advantage_hard receive the intended task-specific prompt contract instead of a generic fallback.\", \"file\": \"src/prompt_builders/resolver.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Fix the persistent simpleqa 0.00 floor in the simple-question branch only. (1) Require the FINAL() answer to be the minimal exact answer \\u2014 the bare fact with no hedging, preamble, restatement, or trailing prose \\u2014 to satisfy exact-match scoring. (2) Extend the uncertainty->lookup path into the simple branch: if the factual answer is not known with confidence, do a quick web_research()/web_search() and then FINAL() the exact answer, rather than hedging or refusing. Do NOT alter the complex-task REPL path, tool semantics, or formatting-constraint adherence.\", \"file\": \"root_lm_system.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Forward OpenAI-compatible tools/tool_choice metadata from chat requests into the ChatPipeline/TaskIR path so the existing tool_use sentinel can produce actual tool calls without changing eval scoring or question pools.\", \"file\": \"src/api/routes/chat.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Improve tool_use suite performance by refining the output format constraints and instruction clarity for tool usage.\", \"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"In resolve_prompt(), add a content-validity guard: after loading orchestration/prompts/<name>.md, if the loaded body is empty, whitespace-only, or fails a basic sanity check (e.g. missing the expected role header / contains leaked planner-journal markers), do NOT return that body \\u2014 fall back to the in-code default constant for that prompt name and log the fallback with provenance (name, path, reason). Single variable: prompt-resolution fallback correctness in resolver.py only. Do NOT edit any .md prompt text, scoring, question pools, model registry, routing flags, baselines, or eval methodology.\", \"file\": \"src/prompt_builders/resolver.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Narrowly escalate low-confidence format-sensitive tasks such as instruction_precision, USACO-like, and mode_advantage_hard instead of accepting cheap-first/frontdoor early exits.\", \"file\": \"src/graph/escalation_helpers.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Narrowly repair tool-use sentinel activation so tool-eligible tool_use tasks are not downgraded to reasoning-only when tools/repl/react_mode are already enabled; keep the change scoped to tool policy gating, not eval scoring or question pools.\", \"file\": \"src/tool_policy.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Normalize hard/format-sensitive suite aliases before escalation decisions so bigcodebench, usaco, instruction_precision, and mode_advantage_hard bypass cheap-first terminal answers and route to the appropriate specialist or architect while preserving the current fast path for coder/math suites.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Optimize frontdoor prompt to improve tool_use and thinking suite performance without regression\", \"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"max_evals\": 50, \"type\": \"gepa_optimize\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Preserve image/attachment payloads and set vision routing metadata when chat requests include visual inputs, so the existing vision/OCR pipeline is reached instead of falling through the text-only path. Text-only requests should be unchanged.\", \"file\": \"src/api/routes/chat.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Preserve original task constraints and expected-output formatting in escalation context so specialists can recover instruction_precision, mode_advantage_hard, bigcodebench, and USACO without changing routing thresholds.\", \"file\": \"src/graph/escalation_helpers.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Preserve the original answer contract during escalation: when building specialist or architect consultation context, carry forward exact output-format constraints, requested final-answer shape, and any no-extra-text requirements from the user prompt. Do not change routing thresholds or force extra escalation; only improve the context handed to already-selected downstream roles.\", \"file\": \"src/graph/escalation_helpers.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Relax only the answer-length ceilings on worker_general: remove the hard 'under 15 words' short-factual cap and the 'under 60 words' open-ended cap, allowing complete answers while KEEPING 'no preamble / no restating the question' and the per-format structure. Single variable = answer-length ceilings. Tests whether the flat general=1.20 (fixed -1.800 gate regression) is length-truncation-driven vs a thin n_baseline=2 artifact.\", \"file\": \"worker_general.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Repair the narrow tool-policy path that can silently collapse explicit CALL()/REPL requests to prose even when tools, repl, and react_mode are enabled. Keep it task-content gated, preserve existing side-effect and allowed-caller checks, and avoid suite-specific logic; this tests whether zero-tool-call tool-use failures are a policy-gate bug.\", \"file\": \"src/tool_policy.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Restructure the frontdoor tool-use instructions from prose into a tighter structured format (Tier-1: 'Tool-use instruction formatting \\u2014 structured vs natural language'). Hypothesis: clearer, lower-token tool-call guidance improves tool-call correctness on the tool_use suite (the planner-prior surface showing nonzero movement) without regressing others, and trims redundant instruction tokens. Rotates off the 3-deep structural_experiment lock-in onto the under-used prompt surface; PromptForge's internal quality gate self-reverts any regression.\", \"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Route hard format-sensitive failures such as instruction_precision, bigcodebench, usaco, and mode_advantage_hard through one specialist or architect escalation instead of accepting low-confidence cheap/frontdoor answers.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Route hard or format-sensitive zero-score suites through one specialist escalation before final answer, without changing model registry or prompt files.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Sharpen debugger system prompt for debugbench: require explicit single-fault localization (cite the exact failing line/symbol and root cause) BEFORE proposing a fix, and emit the minimal patch that addresses only that fault. Do NOT broaden scope, add speculative refactors, or lengthen non-debug reasoning paths. Hypothesis: debugbench declined 3.0->1.76 (and trips the safety gate at -0.203) because the debugger under-localizes and over-patches; precise localization + minimal-patch enforcement should recover debugbench without regressing already-passing coder/livecodebench suites.\", \"file\": \"debugger_system.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Sharpen the debugger system prompt for the declining debugbench/coder/livecodebench cluster: require the model to (1) localize the defect to a specific line/expression and state the failing invariant before proposing a patch, and (2) emit only a minimal, compilable diff that preserves surrounding logic rather than rewriting the function. Do NOT add general verbosity or alter non-debug reasoning paths. Hypothesis: debug/code suites regressed because the debugger under-specifies fault localization and over-rewrites, breaking previously-passing cases; tighter localize-then-minimal-patch guidance should recover the cluster without regressing already-passing suites.\", \"file\": \"debugger_system.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Single mechanism: before returning a cheap/frontdoor answer, detect explicit final-answer or output-format constraints; if the draft visibly violates them, run exactly one same-role cheap format-repair pass that preserves answer content and fixes only the final format. Do not force specialist escalation.\", \"file\": \"src/escalation.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Single mechanism: keep task_token_budget enabled globally, but add a conservative minimum output-token floor for format-sensitive and code-eval requests such as instruction_precision, bigcodebench, usaco, and mode_advantage_hard. Hypothesis: #748 improved quality because these tasks were being truncated; a selective floor should recover quality without the global speed loss from disabling task_token_budget.\", \"file\": \"src/api/routes/chat.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Single-variable test on a new (prompt-content) surface: strengthen the general-purpose worker prompt's task adherence and answer completeness/format discipline for general-suite tasks, without adding tool/scripting/eval-scoring instructions and without touching frontdoor. Diagnostic falsifier: if the general suite still reports the fixed -1.800 (n_baseline=2) after this content change, the regression is baseline-driven and operator-domain; if it clears the gate or the magnitude shifts, the general regression is content-sensitive and this prompt is a real optimization lever.\", \"file\": \"worker_general.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Skip low-value/redundant tool invocations on trivially-answerable queries so simple tasks resolve in fewer tool round-trips. Single-variable: reduce tokens-per-solved-task to lift t/s at the q=2.040 plateau and fill the frontier speed gap (sp 37.6\\u219269.2). No change to routing, escalation, or scoring.\", \"file\": \"src/tool_policy.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Strengthen strict output-format enforcement for constrained-format requests (instruction_precision suite: exact JSON/list/field-order/casing). Add an explicit final-pass format-compliance check that re-emits the answer verbatim to the requested schema before returning. Do NOT lengthen general prose or alter non-format paths.\", \"file\": \"formalizer.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Suppress redundant escalation-to-specialist when the frontdoor quality gate has ALREADY passed for the request (cheap-first\\u2192frontdoor produced an accepted answer). Only escalations that fire despite an already-passing frontdoor result are removed \\u2014 load-bearing escalations (gate-fail, low-confidence, hard suites) are untouched. Hypothesis: this is wasted slow-specialist slot occupancy (coder_esc 10.8 t/s, architects 4-8 t/s vs frontdoor 12.7); removing it advances the speed frontier (#610) and lowers cost at zero quality cost since those requests were already answered acceptably. Expected: escalation_rate \\u2193, speed \\u2191, quality flat.\", \"file\": \"src/graph/escalation_helpers.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Targeted clarity/conciseness fix on a specific frontdoor instruction block (Tier-1) \\u2014 the lowest-tail-risk idle: targeted_fix has a fully clean T0 record (#583/#593, no speed-crater) and the prompt surface has shown no T1-escalation, unlike the structural-toggle surface which just T1-phantom-failed twice (#589 staged_rewards, #595 architect_delegation). PromptForge's gate self-reverts any regression. Rotates off the #594/#595 structural pair to pre-empt the 3-consecutive-structural lock-in.\", \"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"Targeted fix: prevent duplicate specialist/architect escalation only when the request state already contains an accepted final answer from cheap-first/frontdoor and the existing helper would enqueue another escalation for the same request. First verify that an explicit accepted-answer or frontdoor-pass signal exists in this call path; do not alter low-confidence, gate-fail, hard-suite, threshold, or policy behavior. Hypothesis: removing only duplicate post-accept escalation improves speed/cost without quality loss.\", \"file\": \"src/graph/escalation_helpers.py\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"code_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"description\": \"The formalizer prompt enforces strict format compliance (exact JSON structure, field names/order, key casing, list style, delimiters, no-fence rules) by RULE only \\u2014 it contains zero worked examples. Add 1-2 compact few-shot examples showing a format_spec + non-compliant original answer -> the exact compliant reformatted output (e.g. a strict-JSON field-order/casing case and a 'code-only, no fences' case). Examples must only DEMONSTRATE the existing 5 compliance rules verbatim \\u2014 do NOT add, reword, or relax any rule, and do NOT lengthen the operative instructions. Hypothesis: instruction_precision and other strict-format outputs miss verbatim schema adherence because the model has rules but no concrete pattern to imitate; grounded few-shot exemplars should raise format compliance without regressing non-format paths or speed.\", \"file\": \"formalizer.md\", \"mutation\": \"few_shot_evolution\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
    "{\"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"max_evals\": 50, \"type\": \"gepa_optimize\"}": 1,
    "{\"file\": \"frontdoor.md\", \"mutation\": \"targeted_fix\", \"type\": \"prompt_mutation\"}": 1,
